<title>USA: Gabelli group cuts Moog Inc stake.</title>
<headline>Gabelli group cuts Moog Inc stake.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-02-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>A group led by New York investment manager Mario Gabelli said on Monday that it cut its stake in Moog Inc. to 568,000 class A common shares, or 10.53 percent of the total outstanding.</p>
<p>In a filing with the Securities and Exchange Commission, the group said it sold 47,800 shares between Dec. 9, 1996, and Feb. 6, 1997, at prices ranging from $23.5313 to $25.6765 a share.</p>
<p>The group said it holds its stake in Moog for investment purposes.</p>
